{
  "id": "interrupted-time-series-design",
  "term": "interrupted time-series design",
  "definition": "An interrupted time-series design is a way of evaluating a change by tracking measures repeatedly over time and then examining how they shift after a clearly defined intervention or policy is introduced. It is used to look for immediate changes or changes in the pattern over time following that interruption.",
